@page "/Devlogs/v0_2_RCS_RERL"
@using RocketEngineDocs.Components
@inherits RocketEngineDocs.Components.DevlogBase

@code {

    public override DevlogHeader Header => new()
    {
        Title = "RCS & RERL",
        Version = "v0.2",
        Summary = "Lighting, textures, GLTF support, and major rendering improvements.",
        Url = "Devlogs/v0_2_RCS_RERL",
        Order = 2,
        Date = new DateTime(2026, 4, 10),
        IsWip = false,
        Libraries = ["RCS", "RERL"]
    };
}

<DevlogHeaderComponent Meta="Header" />

<p>
    Version v0.2 focuses on making Rocket Engine feel more like a usable engine rather than a boring old tech demo.
    v0.2 add lighting, model loading, and a more complete rendering pipeline. As well as some backend stuff to
    strengthen the engine so future systems have a solid base to build on.
</p>

<DevlogImage Src="Images/v0.2/scene.png"
             Alt="Scene"
             Caption="A look at the new lighting and GLTF model rendering in v0.2." />

<h2>Overview</h2>

<p>
    The main focus of v0.2 was usability. This meant replacing temporary systems, adding missing rendering
    features, and improving the workflow for building scenes. The biggest changes include a proper lighting
    system, albedo texture support, and GLTF model loading with basic a hierarchy return system.
</p>

<ul>
    <li>New lighting system (point, spot, directional).</li>
    <li>Albedo Texture and color material support. PBR is to come.</li>
    <li>GLTF scene loading (hierarchy, transforms, glb).</li>
    <li>Improved G‑Buffer and shading pipeline.</li>
    <li>OBJ support removed in favor of GLTF.</li>
</ul>

<div class="devlog-box">

    <h2 class="lib-heading lib-rcs">RCS | Rocket Control System v0.2</h2>

    <p>
        RCS wasn't given as much love as RERL this update, but it did get Transform listeners, arbitrary entity data,
        and an engine wide logger.
    </p>

    <h3>Completed in v0.2</h3>

    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Transform Listeners</strong><br />
            Components can follow an entity’s position or direction automatically, useful for lights and effects.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Entity Data Storage</strong><br />
            Entities can store arbitrary key/value data, enabling easy procedural animation, and other cool stuff.
        </li>
        
        <li>
            <strong>Logger</strong><br />
            The new logger can output logs, warnings, and errors to the console and or to a file.
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="devlog-box">

    <h2 class="lib-heading lib-rerl">RERL | Rocket Engine Rendering Library v0.2</h2>

    <p>
        RERL saw the most change in v0.2. The rendering pipeline has been expanded to support lighting,
        albedo textures, and model loading. Many of the temporary systems from v0.1 were replaced with more
        complete versions.
    </p>

    <h3>Completed in v0.2</h3>

    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Lighting System</strong><br />
            Support for point, spot, and directional lights, including smooth edge clamping and global lights. With cluster shading optimizations.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Albedo Texture & Color Material Support</strong><br />
            Models can now use albedo textures & color materials. PBR materials are yet to come.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>GLTF Model Loading</strong><br />
            GLTF support. OBJ loading was removed.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Improved G‑Buffer</strong><br />
            A more complete deferred rendering layout with position, normal, albedo, and depth attachments.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Shader Improvements</strong><br />
            Shader type categories, and better helper includes for prelight and post‑process passes.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Post‑Processing Enhancements</strong><br />
            The post‑processing system from v0.1 was refined and integrated more cleanly into the pipeline.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Compute Shader Support</strong><br />
            A new <code>Compute</code> class allows GPU compute workloads with a simple API.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        With these changes, RERL can now render complex scenes with many lights and albedo textured models.
        The pipeline is still evolving, and needed features will soon be added.
    </p>

</div>